{"title":"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(combinatorial)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (combinatorial)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(computational/&#39;bash&#39;)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (computational/'bash')</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9b25f4d911ea474d71e21a95ced314e6520e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lbrace1,2,3,\\ldots,10\\rbrace$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of sets of two non-empty disjoint subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. (Disjoint sets are defined as sets that have no common elements.) Find the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28combinatorial.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(combinatorial)\">Solution 1 (combinatorial)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (combinatorial)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the two disjoint subsets be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e70681f072555598d84baa3ffcf2d0c58979b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\mathcal{S}\\setminus\\left(A \\cup B\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is disjoint from both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and every element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, if not contained in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, is necessarily contained in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). This means every element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9790fd9e148fb6684cf730f12a84f075a0737190.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in \\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> satisfies exactly one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47d50a2dbe1586a3a6363fef5b6ca9815f74c510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6ef56ef9eed9f6d965db6981054b3c8f6679247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0bfc2010a37ca5ee8d8553f74881b8e12ea4bfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, i.e. for each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements, we have to independently choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subsets into which to place it. Hence there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c6857bf408376c55c9fa09141f94834a186034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{10}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> ways to partition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> into disjoint subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>However, we must exclude those partitions in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> (or both) is empty. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e3236a24240fb6689c596f92015a9e46c9e6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735c3c6314265234a2e5813316e0f1528e6ec022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S} = B \\cup C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />, then we have to place each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> into either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b2422eb1e019642032c00b0c5d5982903fe45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> such partitions (similarly to above). By symmetry, the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d27c56b4e82d1f4324efa55f3e6e9a150daf81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\emptyset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d49dc8a9e0e608e90039d74b9b2b84e1971a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S} = A \\cup C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> also gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b2422eb1e019642032c00b0c5d5982903fe45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> partitions, so we need to subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b2422eb1e019642032c00b0c5d5982903fe45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> twice from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c6857bf408376c55c9fa09141f94834a186034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{10}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. But then the partition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957eae79760b60b223c549c378c6c80de2348181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = B = \\emptyset, \\mathcal{S} = C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />, which falls within <i>both</i> of the above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases, would be double-counted in the subtraction, so we must add it back. \n</p><p>Accordingly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c2ad17607fd030d1fc0514c825852510c6c233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3^{10}-2\\cdot2^{10}+1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" /> possible ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> (or equivalently, partitions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />). Each pair has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible orders (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, being disjoint, obviously cannot be the same), so the above expression counts each <i>unordered</i> set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c3f67cac86cb745932673bc5aa6c04538d9b9e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{A,B\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> exactly twice. Thus, finally, we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/60806973967ab7d3bb8ac991ca292b26ac4dba00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(3^{10}-2\\cdot2^{10}+1\\right) = 28501 \\equiv \\boxed{501} \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"423\" height=\"38\" />.  \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28computational.2F.27bash.27.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(computational/'bash')\">Solution 2 (computational/'bash')</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (computational/&#39;bash&#39;)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, let the two disjoint subsets be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. We observe that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> elements, which can be chosen in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/024069a279760792915d098b2b0ff7293c49b299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{10}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"48\" height=\"55\" /> ways, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f36a647c729604705cdb95e28b60b90bf0716d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10-p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> remaining elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a281826fab0dc40a4eb1bbf99c6f1c19afbe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> from which to choose the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> elements, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930e02967678ef115d9f49f83e437e1c0eb790f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq q \\leq 10-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, and similarly to above, these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> elements can be chosen in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef78f00e47771fc4853bbbcbb70e302a0ce8d70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{10-p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"80\" height=\"55\" /> ways. Moreover, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must both be non-empty, we require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a51ce59afdd4b396899db46e9ca0f9f3a44c321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8bccfc45b74f1ba906e9492d9b11bb1c5395bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-p \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307fa5502e10ec10bcf2bead581560ae882aa0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq p \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. It follows that for each fixed value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the number of possible ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/5006f1cd2a0af378ead68f57da352bf0fdc72256.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\binom{10}{p}\\sum_{q=1}^{10-p}\\binom{10-p}{q} &amp;= \\binom{10}{p}\\sum_{q=1}^{10-p}\\binom{10-p}{q}1^q 1^{(10-p)-q} \\\\ &amp;= \\binom{10}{p}\\left(\\sum_{q=0}^{10-p}\\binom{10-p}{q}1^q 1^{(10-p)-q} - \\binom{10-p}{0}\\cdot 1^0 \\cdot 1^{(10-p)-0}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\binom{10}{p}\\left(\\left(1+1\\right)^{10-p} - 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1\\right) \\qquad \\text{(by the binomial theorem)} \\\\ &amp;= \\binom{10}{p}\\left(2^{10-p}-1\\right),\\end{align*}\" width=\"660\" height=\"238\" /> and summing this expression over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307fa5502e10ec10bcf2bead581560ae882aa0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq p \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> will therefore give the total number of such ordered pairs.\n</p><p>Just like in Solution 1, counting ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is equivalent to counting each unordered set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c3f67cac86cb745932673bc5aa6c04538d9b9e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{A,B\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> exactly twice, so we deduce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/1411d7d2741671a650cb331d84b603a1affeede1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}2n &amp;= \\sum_{p=1}^{9}\\binom{10}{p}\\left(2^{10-p}-1\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\sum_{p=1}^{9}\\binom{10}{p}1^p 2^{10-p} - \\sum_{p=1}^{9}\\binom{10}{p}1^p 1^{10-p} \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\sum_{p=0}^{10}\\binom{10}{p}1^p 2^{10-p} - \\binom{10}{0} \\cdot 1^0 \\cdot 2^{10-0} - \\binom{10}{10} \\cdot 1^{10} \\cdot 2^{10-10}\\right) \\\\ &amp;\\phantom{=} -\\left(\\sum_{p=0}^{10}\\binom{10}{p}1^p 1^{10-p} - \\binom{10}{0} \\cdot 1^0 \\cdot 1^{10-0} - \\binom{10}{10} \\cdot 1^{10} \\cdot 1^{10-10}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\left(1+2\\right)^{10} - 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2^{10} - 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1\\right) - \\left(\\left(1+1\\right)^{10} - 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1\\right) \\\\ &amp;\\phantom{=} \\text{(again by the binomial theorem)} \\\\ &amp;= 3^{10}-2^{10}-1-2^{10}+1+1 \\\\ &amp;= 3^{10} - 2 \\cdot 2^{10} + 1.\\end{align*}\" width=\"559\" height=\"359\" /> Hence, as in Solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/60806973967ab7d3bb8ac991ca292b26ac4dba00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(3^{10}-2\\cdot2^{10}+1\\right) = 28501 \\equiv \\boxed{501} \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"423\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.1\">Solution 2.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Continue until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32d0c05d7adb9713af206eb2478db6e207b4794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k} \\cdot (2^{k-1} -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"170\" height=\"56\" />. is obtained. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed961f959d399185e851663637a502c65f4bc51e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k} \\cdot 2^{k-1} - \\binom{10}{k}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b629518e7f186594580c8a224d6f8a4bb0248ae6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k} \\cdot 2^{k-1} - \\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Subset Theorem on the right sum,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2db7cc393872799379ac3f034ce1eb56d7266d91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k} \\cdot 2^{k-1} - (2^{10} - 1)\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Left sum rearrangement,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/a/6ea7cc04fb211ca565124248764cd7cbd5b90b0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sum_{k=1}^{10} \\binom{10}{k} \\cdot 2^{k}) - (2^{10} - 1)\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Binomial Theorem\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/458d32f8177613664c24ff8beeb287327f22349b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (1+2)^{10} - 1 = 3^{10} - 1\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>So \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6de1bb53fae1ad4c5cde0e394b50a484d75729.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (3^{10}-1) - 2^{10} + 1 \\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>is desired. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3325c9c6289d03f5b262314a657b4e16699c09ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (3^{10} - 1)  \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"196\" height=\"38\" /> is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd57c227e97671bb8bf76a8e25ce0aeaffa3eb14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$524$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbe64cc93ad4ae277c51cf983fa61500ad469b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$524 - 2^{10} + 1 \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />  or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0f6fb7c384327937378280fb3146ffeac7415b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500+1 \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e44b7de8ba14e987cb94543781629818c089c22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Overall this is much simpler than computing the behemoth above.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II\" title=\"2002 AIME II\">2002 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017015013\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 532/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17572/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.028      1 -total\n 61.20%    7.973      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.17%    4.842      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3120:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017015013 and revision id 283552. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}